	(text "DIP PULL-UPS: 100k, NOT the 1M the review asked for.\nThe review said \"increase pull-ups for DIP to 1 MOhm\". The intent - stop burning\ncurrent in a switch that sits closed for the whole match - is right, but 1M does\nnot survive the STM32H7 input spec:\n\n   STM32H7 I/O leakage is +/- 1 uA max.  VIH = 0.7 x VDD = 2.31 V.\n      10k  -> worst-case high 3.29 V  (2.0 mA per closed switch, 12 mA for six)\n      100k -> worst-case high 3.20 V  (33 uA per switch, 198 uA for six)   <-- chosen\n      1M   -> worst-case high 2.30 V  -- BELOW VIH. Reads as logic 0. FAILS.\n\nAt 1M a single leaky pin, a fingerprint, or any flux residue across the switch\nflips a robot-ID bit, and the failure is intermittent and field-only. 100k drops\nthe current by 10x versus the original 10k while keeping ~0.9 V of noise margin.\n\nThese are read once at boot, so there is no speed argument for a lower value.\nIf the ID is ever read continuously, add a 100nF to GND at each pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 33.02 271.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
